Maintainer: Farhan Tahir <farhan.003@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ftahirops/xtop
Description: Incident-first root-cause analysis console for Linux
 v0.50.0 — The correctness release: adversarially-verified RCA engine
 audit (27 findings, 7 structural classes, all fixed) plus a 22-page /
 486-parameter verification of every displayed value against live
 /proc, ss, df, and cgroup ground truth.
 .
   RCA engine correctness
     * specific-cause narratives require their defining evidence
       (no "hypervisor steal" without steal, no "swap thrashing"
       on non-swapping hosts)
     * run queue from instantaneous procs_running, not Load1
     * confidence capped by evidence strength
     * WHO always agrees with WHY (slab leaks blame the kernel)
     * pinned RCA renders one consistent frame
     * Proxmox/journal/config-drift evidence flows into scoring
       before the verdict is finalized
     * unverified verdicts labeled; lean mode surfaces coverage
 .
   Reporting accuracy
     * LVM/RAID disk throughput/IOPS/top-writer no longer doubled
     * MySQL 8 event scheduler no longer trips a bogus kill-query CRIT
     * runtime census scans all of /proc; app memory uses full-tree RSS
     * vhost-only web servers probe as WARN, not down
     * partial disk scans labeled; warm-up shows dashes, not zeros
 .
   New
     * DiskGuard TOP DIRECTORIES (du-style rollups)
     * Apps Runtime column (docker/k8s/native) + readable Ranks
